            "review_title": "Review at Valhalla Grill Xuan Dieu",
            "review_text": "JSTrip_77\nSarajevo, Bosnia and Herzegovina1194 contributions\n0\nGreat Inexpensive Burgers and Pulled Pork!\nJan 2019 • Couples\nIt's possible that this location was previously a restaurant called Country Pub and Grill or something. This is one of at least two locations of Valhalla Grill in Hanoi. This location is on To Ngoc Van and is the one that I've visited. We've been meaning to try this place for some time now and finally did. And, while I loved what I got, I had extreme food envy for the pulled pork. In fact, I WILL eat that pulled pork sandwich sometime this week (or even weekend!!). My Vietnamese pork sandwich was very good too but it was nothing compared to the juicy, messy goodness of the pulled pork. Honestly, even the falafel was really good here. (The fries were crispy and not at all greasy.)\n\nThe staff was really friendly and helpful with our meals and also helped us with our Vietnamese. It's a great neighborhood place and I'll be back soon.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 4, 2019",
